# The Amazon SQS-compatible message queue service (services/sqs/,
# .kiro/specs/sqs-compatible-queues/). Sourced from the top-level Kconfig's
# "Service Modules" menu.

config SQS
	bool "Amazon SQS-compatible message queue service"
	default n
	depends on OPENSSL
	help
	  Builds the services/sqs/ module: an Amazon SQS-compatible queue
	  service that unmodified AWS SDKs, the AWS CLI, JMS, Spring Cloud
	  AWS, Celery and Kombu can point at, with each queue's messages,
	  visibility and FIFO state kept in Kythira's Raft groups on the
	  persistent key-value engine. So far the module holds the pinned
	  botocore model, the generated operation table, the coverage check
	  and the sqs_node placeholder (task 1); the gateway, front end and
	  queue state machine follow. It needs IAM's core SigV4 and authorizer
	  headers, not the IAM module. OpenSSL is needed for SigV4, MD5
	  digests and receipt-handle HMACs. Off by default like every new
	  module (services/README.md). See .kiro/specs/sqs-compatible-queues/.
